{"name":"Hyacinth Ice","hex":"#c8c8d2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hyacinth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any bulbous plant of the genus Hyacinthus, native to the Mediterranean and South Africa.","A variety of zircon, ranging in color from brown, orange, reddish-brown and yellow; a jacinth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hyacinth"},{"term":"ice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Icelandic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water in frozen (solid) form.","Any frozen volatile chemical, such as ammonia or carbon dioxide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hyacinth","blocks":[{"text":"Hyacinthus is a genus of bulbous herbs and spring-blooming perennials. They are fragrant flowering plants in the family Asparagaceae, subfamily Scilloideae and are commonly called hyacinths. The genus is native predominantly to the Eastern Mediterranean region from the south of Turkey to the Palestine region, although naturalized more widely."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Hyacinth_-_Anglesey_Abbey.jpg/330px-Hyacinth_-_Anglesey_Abbey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyacinth","wikidata":"Q158758"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%2